  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:93443",
  "description": "Mozilla Thunderbird is a standalone mail and newsgroup client.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * libexpat: denial of service via crafted XML input (CVE-2026-45186)\n  * firefox: Mitigation bypass in the Enterprise Policies component (CVE-2026-109764)\n  * firefox: Spoofing issue in the DOM: Web Serial component (CVE-2026-109770)\n  * firefox: Mitigation bypass in the File Handling component (CVE-2026-109783)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Privilege escalation in the Application Update component (CVE-2026-109704)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the XML component (CVE-2026-109718)\n  * firefox: Information disclosure in the PDF Viewer component (CVE-2026-109742)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine component (CVE-2026-109715)\n  * firefox: firefox: Sandbox escape via incorrect boundary conditions in Win32 widget (CVE-2026-109740)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Storage: IndexedDB component (CVE-2026-109706)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Crash Reporting component (CVE-2026-109713)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-109724)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to uninitialized memory in the DOM: Web Serial component (CVE-2026-109745)\n  * firefox: Mitigation bypass in the File Handling component (CVE-2026-109782)\n  * firefox: Information disclosure, privilege escalation in the Security: Process Sandboxing component (CVE-2026-109709)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape, site isolation issue due to incorrect boundary conditions, use-after-free in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109705)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Audio/Video: Playback component (CVE-2026-109738)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to race condition in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109757)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Storage: Bucket File System component (CVE-2026-109741)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109729)\n  * firefox: Other issue in the DOM: File component (CVE-2026-109744)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine component (CVE-2026-109716)\n  * firefox: Race condition, use-after-free in the Graphics: CanvasWebGL component (CVE-2026-109719)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the Layout component (CVE-2026-109753)\n  * firefox: Integer overflow in the Layout: Text and Fonts component (CVE-2026-109723)\n  * firefox: Privilege escalation in the DOM: Navigation component (CVE-2026-109756)\n  * firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109733)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Mitigation bypass in the DOM: Security component (CVE-2026-109734)\n  * firefox: Mitigation bypass in the File Handling component (CVE-2026-109763)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to incorrect boundary conditions in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109708)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Bindings (WebIDL) component (CVE-2026-109717)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Workers component (CVE-2026-109752)\n  * firefox: Race condition in the XPCOM component (CVE-2026-109776)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109707)\n  * firefox: Mitigation bypass in the Networking: HTTP component (CVE-2026-109760)\n  * firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript: WebAssembly component (CVE-2026-109720)\n  * firefox: Information disclosure in the Storage: IndexedDB component (CVE-2026-109777)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the SVG component (CVE-2026-109726)\n  * firefox: Integer overflow in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-109730)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Audio/Video component (CVE-2026-109727)\n  * firefox: Mitigation bypass in the Enterprise Policies component (CVE-2026-109737)\n  * firefox: Mitigation bypass in the Enterprise Policies component (CVE-2026-109766)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Streams component (CVE-2026-109732)\n  * firefox: Site isolation issue in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109759)\n  * firefox: Privilege escalation in the WebExtensions component (CVE-2026-109778)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the SVG component (CVE-2026-109762)\n  * firefox: Race condition, use-after-free in the Graphics: Text component (CVE-2026-109765)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the DOM: Editor component (CVE-2026-109754)\n  * firefox: Information disclosure in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109751)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-109725)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to uninitialized memory in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-109712)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Graphics: Canvas2D component (CVE-2026-109711)\n  * firefox: Frame poisoning in the Layout component (CVE-2026-109736)\n  * firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109722)\n  * firefox: Information disclosure in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109767)\n  * firefox: Denial-of-service in the WebRTC component (CVE-2026-109775)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Animation component (CVE-2026-109728)\n  * firefox: Denial-of-service in the Printing: Output component (CVE-2026-109781)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the Graphics: Text component (CVE-2026-109710)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Incorrect boundary conditions in the Graphics: Canvas2D component (CVE-2026-109731)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109721)\n  * firefox: Privilege escalation in the Panning and Zooming component (CVE-2026-109743)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Thunderbird ESR 153 rebase [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:RHEL-175199)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
